{"text": "thankful", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">thankful</i>, from Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">\u00feancful</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">\u00feancfull</i> (\u201cthoughtful, pleasing, agreeable, pleasant, thankful, grateful\u201d), equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">thank</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-ful</i>. Compare Old High German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"goh\">undankfol</i> (\u201cunthankful, ungrateful\u201d).\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "Showing appreciation or gratitude.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(obsolete) Obtaining or deserving thanks; thankworthy.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["IPA", "/\u02c8\u03b8\u00e6\u014bkf\u0259l/"]]}